autonumber "<b>0"
skinparam ParticipantPadding 4
skinparam BoxPadding 4
skinparam maxMessageSize 320
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Sequence diagram — AI assistance (1/2): maintenance ticket triage

actor "Reporter" as R
box "Front end · React" #F3F7FC
boundary "MaintenancePage" as UI
end box
box "Back end · NestJS" #F3F8F4
control "AiController" as AC
participant "MaintenanceTriage\nService" as T <<service>>
participant "OpenAiService" as O <<service>>
participant "PrismaService" as PR <<repository>>
end box
box "Data" #F7F4FB
database "**PostgreSQL**" as DB
end box
box "External" #F4F5F6
participant "LLM provider\n(OpenAI-compatible)" as LLM <<external>>
end box

R -> UI : title and description
UI -> AC ++ : POST /ai/maintenance/triage
AC -> T ++ : triage(user, { title, description })
== 1. category and priority ==
  opt API key configured
    T -> O ++ : chatJson(text, allowed categories and priorities)
    O -> LLM : POST /chat/completions
    LLM --> O : { category, priority, reason }
    return parsed answer, or null
  end
  alt both values belong to the enumerations
    T -> T : source = "model"
  else invented value, no answer, or no key
    T -> T : keyword classifier, source = "keywords"
  end
== 2. suggested technician and past fixes ==
opt caller can assign (SUPER_ADMIN, CLIENT_ADMIN, MANAGER)
    T -> PR : active technicians, and their resolved\nand open tickets in this category
    PR -> DB : SELECT users, maintenance_tickets
    T -> T : score = 10 × resolved − 6 × open\n(tie: lighter load first)
    T -> PR : 3 latest resolved tickets of this category\nin the company's buildings
end
== 3. the reporter decides ==
T --> AC : category, priority, reason,\nsuggestedAssignee, similar, source
deactivate T
AC --> UI : 201 Created
deactivate AC
UI --> R : show the suggestion
opt the reporter accepts it
  R -> UI : Apply / Assign to them
  UI -> UI : fill in category, priority, assignee
end
ref over UI, PR
  **Submit the ticket**: POST /maintenance → MaintenanceService.create():
  403 for a renter whose company neither booked nor leased the space;
  otherwise ticket ASSIGNED (assignee given) or OPEN, space MAINTENANCE
  if URGENT or EMERGENCY, assignee notified and e-mailed.
end ref

note over T, LLM
  The model proposes; it never decides. The technician
  comes from ticket history, and submitting a ticket
  never depends on the model.
end note
@enduml
